{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/436066-help-boon-vs-knack-issue","id":436066,"title":"Help boon vs knack issue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-10T12:52:17-07:00","id":436066,"title":"Help boon vs knack issue","content":"Solipsistic Well\u2013Being - The philosophy of solipsism holds that only the self exists. Accordingly, if a solipsist isn\u2019t aware of something, that something doesn\u2019t exist. With this Knack, a Scion applies this odd philosophy to damage that surprises her. For a single attack that the Scion doesn\u2019t see, hear or otherwise perceive coming, the Scion can spend a point of Legend and a point of Willpower to completely ignore it as if it never happened (thereby suffering no damage from it). Of course the attack does actually happen\u2014any ammunition used is spent, onlookers might be covered with the Scion\u2019s blood, the would-be assassin might be standing right there holding a dripping knife\u2014but such concerns are immaterial to the Scion victim.<br /> <br /> Paralyzing confusion - This Boon turns a person\u2019s rational thoughts into seething, chaotic noise. On a successful activation roll, the victim freezes in place, suddenly unable to think, speak or act. He\u2019s unaware of what goes on around him, and he has no memory of the moments before or after the use of this Boon.<br /> <br /> So here's the basic scene. My pc was hit with Paralyzing confusion for 9 rounds of derp. Then another NPC ran up and started attacking me while i was Derped. Since the power freezes, no thought, no speech or act, I don't know that an attack is coming does my Solipsistic Well-Being work and Can i spend the Will and Legend to activate it? ST and I got into a debate over it he agreed that i wouldn't see the attack coming, but I also wouldn't be able to spend the will and Legend to activate.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, comments, charges of heresy?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance<br /> <br /> ~D <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3529-dracosilver","name":"Dracosilver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:22:42-07:00","id":436261,"title":"","content":"Hm....in my own game I would have to go with that you can't use the knack<br /> <br /> SImply put because paralyzing touch makes you blank out, you can't do any sort of actions physically or mentally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:22:51-07:00","id":436263,"title":"","content":"I'd let you use Solipsistic Well-Being. It works on attacks you aren't aware of. Paralyzing Confusion makes you unaware of attacks. It's not like it's going to do much if you get derped for 9 turns... you can only use Solipsistic Well-Being once per scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T23:55:44-07:00","id":436783,"title":"","content":"In my opinion if you didn't see the Boon use coming (and one could argue that you have no way of perceiving it coming as there isn't exactly a light show, there's just the desire for it to happen), SWB may have been useable against the initial attack. You'd be ready for the follow up slash-fest so it's no use there but unless you were in the thick of things the Chaos attack itself may have been a valid target for SWB and you may not have had to be stunned at all.<br /> <br /> Of course if you did, then I'd allow it for the first attack, as it's more a reflexive action (like breathing) than a directed one (such as firing up, say, Telescopic Senses). Then you're in for eight rounds of slashy-slashy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}